     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am currently using shiny on a machine B that cannot be reached via internet (only LAN access). I would like to expose it via server A that can be reached via the internet.<br>The setup I currently employ is based on proxies and rewrites on server A as follows:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#&lt;LocationMatch &quot;^/SHINY&quot;&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#       AuthType        Basic</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#        AuthName       &quot;SHINY&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#       AuthUserFile    /.../.htpasswd_SHINY</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#       Require         valid-user</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#&lt;/LocationMatch&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">RewriteCond</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">HTTP</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Upgrade</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">websocket<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">RewriteRule</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SHINY</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/(.*)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ws</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//...:3838/$1 [P,L]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rewritecond</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">HTTP</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Upgrade</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">!=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">websocket<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">RewriteRule</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SHINY</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/(.*)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//...:3838/$1 [P,L]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">ProxyPass</span><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SHINY</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//...:3838/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">ProxyPassReverse</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SHINY</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//...:3838/</span></div></code></div><br>It is working but if I uncomment the LocationMatch section, after asking for the credentials the system is blocked on &#39;Connecting ...&#39;<br>Is this due to the system asking continuously for authorization without showing any window?<br>The strange thing (to me) is that within the LAN it keeps on working correctly: credentials are asked for at the beginning, everything loads fine afterwards.<br><br>Thanks for any hint!<br></div>"
